# Monorepo scope constraints

You are strictly confined to these directories unless the user explicitly expands scope:

- `apps/app/`
- `apps/api/`
- `apps/interview/`
- `packages/design-system/`

- NEVER index, read, grep, search, or edit files under other `apps/*` folders (`storybook`, `with-solid`, `testing-lab`, etc.).
- NEVER index, read, grep, search, or edit files under other `packages/*` folders unless the user explicitly asks.
- Treat all other apps and packages as completely out of scope to save token limits.
- Prefer targeted searches within the allowed paths only (e.g. `apps/app/**`, `apps/api/**`, `apps/interview/**`, `packages/design-system/**`).
- If a task appears to require code outside this scope, stop and ask the user before reading or changing those paths.

Root workspace config (`package.json`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, `turbo.json`, `biome.jsonc`) may be read when needed for commands — do not implement product features there.

This aligns with `.cursorignore` at the repo root.
